{
 "manufacturer": "Yaskawa",
 "manufacturer_slug": "yaskawa",
 "model": "iQpump drive (P7U-based, legacy) - Modbus RTU",
 "model_slug": "iqpump-p7u",
 "short_model": "iQpump (legacy)",
 "aliases": [
  "iQpump",
  "CIMR-P7U iQpump",
  "iQpump Drive"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive (pump)",
 "applies_to": "Legacy Yaskawa iQpump drives built on the P7U platform (CIMR-P7U...), per user manual TM.iQp.01, using the built-in RS-422/485 terminals R+/R-/S+/S-.",
 "summary": "The original Yaskawa iQpump is a pump-application drive based on the P7 platform with an embedded Modbus RTU slave on terminals R+/R-/S+/S-. Commands go to hex registers 0001H-000FH, status and fault words are read from 0020H upward, and parameters have their own hex Modbus addresses in Appendix A. This map covers the command block, status/fault words, PI levels, pump monitors, fault history codes and the b1/H5 setup parameters.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 31,
  "baud": 9600,
  "parity": "None",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "hex 0-based",
  "note": "Register numbers are hex and are sent unchanged: the 03H example reads from start address 00 20 (drive status), and the 10H example writes 0001H (run forward) and 0002H (0258H = 600 for 60.0 Hz) starting at 00 01. Parameters use the hex Modbus address in Appendix A (b1-01 = 0180H, H5-01 = 0425H)."
 },
 "default_word_order": null,
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "iQpump Drive User Manual",
  "doc_number": "TM.iQp.01",
  "revision_date": null,
  "url": "https://www.yaskawa.com/delegate/getAttachment?documentId=TM.iQp.01&cmd=documents&documentName=TM.iQp.01.pdf",
  "pages": "Appendix D pp. 207-219 (D.1 setup and H5 table p. 210, function examples pp. 212-213, data tables pp. 214-218); Appendix A monitor list pp. 190-192, fault trace/history pp. 193-194, d/E params p. 170"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Monitor registers 0023H/0024H and U1 monitors are listed raw where the manual gives no resolution or unit for them (only U1-90/U1-91 state 0.1 resolution and the PI levels state 10 = 1 %).",
  "Left out because the manual prints no units or resolution: 0025H output voltage, 0026H output current, 0027H output power, 0028H torque reference, 0031H DC bus voltage, and the 0040H-0067H U1 monitor block and U2 snapshot values.",
  "Fault code numbers for U2/U3 registers are not tabulated in this manual's Modbus appendix, so no value list is given.",
  "H5-08 (protocol select: Modbus, APOGEE FLN, Metasys N2) is referenced in the H5 table but its Modbus address is not printed there; it is not listed.",
  "Broadcast (address 0) accepts only 0001H with its own bit layout (bit 0 run, bit 1 reverse, bit 4 external error, bit 5 fault reset, bits C-E S5-S7) and 0002H (30000 = 100 %).",
  "U3-07 is printed as 009BH in the fault history table, which breaks the 0094H-0097H sequence; the elapsed-time registers are not included."
 ],
